From 3ee7e1ae2b668cddddf56059823ad789aec6fbb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:25:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Fix #3, #28: central sync keeps each twin's phase and
 checks folder names

Apply matched every local project on the same Helix/Procore connection
and took FoldersOverride and Scope from a remote change with overwrite,
so a colleague editing their Base Build entry turned this PC's Tenant
Fit-Out twin into Base Build (and swapped its returned folder).

- Discipline choices still merge into every twin.
- FoldersOverride and Scope are taken only from the same tracker project
  (same id) or a twin whose phase already matches; Scope.Phase never
  changes across different ids.
- A remote FoldersOverride is taken only when FolderLayout.Validate()
  passes and the RFI and Submittal folders are plain names (no drive,
  share or rooted path). The returned folder may still be a full path,
  since a shared returned folder is set for everyone that way; every
  move it leads to still goes through the preview.

Tests (CentralTests): existing shared-choices test now uses matching
phases; BB+TFO twins on one Helix connection receive a remote BB change
and the TFO twin keeps its phase and folders; unsafe overrides
(Z:\, \\server, .., duplicate names) are ignored while choices still
merge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
